  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{P}$ be the point of intersection of the lines $\\frac{x-2}{1}=\\frac{y-4}{5}=\\frac{z-2}{1}$ and $\\frac{x-3}{2}=\\frac{y-2}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{2}$. Then, the shortest distance of P from the line $4 x=2 y=z$ is",
